# Authorization: RBAC and Request Access Rules

## Scope

Applies to all tenant-scoped authorization and request-level access decisions.

## Authorization Model

The system uses two authorization layers:
1. tenant RBAC permissions
2. request-level access rules

Both layers must always be enforced server-side.

## Tenant RBAC Roles

Default tenant roles:
- OWNER
- ADMIN
- FINANCE
- MEMBER

Do not assume platform-level administrative roles are part of tenant RBAC.

## Role Responsibilities

### OWNER
Full tenant control.

### ADMIN
Broad tenant management permissions except billing-sensitive operations unless explicitly granted.

### FINANCE
Can manage:
- requests
- approvals
- payments
- operational finance workflows

Cannot manage:
- tenant role architecture
- billing ownership unless explicitly granted

### MEMBER
Limited access focused on request creation and request participation according to granted access.

## Permission Catalog

### Tenant admin
- `tenant.audit.read`
- `tenant.billing.manage`
- `tenant.settings.manage`
- `tenant.roles.read`
- `tenant.roles.manage`
- `tenant.users.read`
- `tenant.users.invite`
- `tenant.users.manage`
- `tenant.users.disable`

### Requests
- `tenant.requests.create`
- `tenant.requests.read_all`
- `tenant.requests.close`
- `tenant.requests.share`
- `tenant.requests.link`
- `tenant.requests.export`
- `tenant.requests.comment`

### Evidence
- `tenant.evidence.add`

### Approvals
- `tenant.approvals.assign_internal`
- `tenant.approvals.assign_external`
- `tenant.approvals.remind`

### Payments
- `tenant.payments.manage`

## Platform-Level vs Tenant-Level Authority

Platform-level administrative authority is separate from tenant RBAC.

Rules:
- platform roles must not be confused with tenant roles
- tenant permissions must still be evaluated explicitly for tenant-scoped operations
- elevated platform endpoints must remain isolated and intentional

## Request Access Rules

A user may access a request if any condition is true:
- the user created the request
- the user is an assigned internal participant
- the user has shared access
- the user has `tenant.requests.read_all`

## Required Helper

Use a shared helper for request access checks.

Example:
`canAccessRequest({ tenantId, userId, requestId })`

All request endpoints must rely on shared authorization helpers rather than duplicating access logic.

## Creator-Only Approval Management

Members can assign approvers only for requests they created unless broader permission is granted.

Rules:
- creator may manage approvals for their own request
- users with `tenant.approvals.assign_internal` may manage internal approval assignment according to policy
- approval execution itself is governed by actual assignment and workflow state

## External Approver Access

External approver access must be narrowly scoped.

Rules:
- external approver access grants access only to the approval artifact or workflow step intended
- external approval access must not imply tenant membership
- external actors must never gain broad tenant visibility

## Consistency Rules

Unauthorized users must not learn whether a protected request exists.

Prefer returning:
- `404`

when concealment is the safer behavior.

## Authorization Helper Discipline

Use shared authorization helpers for:
- tenant permission checks
- request access checks
- creator-only actions
- concealed resource responses